+# Performance history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+Measured with the release benchmark harness on a synthetic store containing 5,000
+records and 15,000 cues, using 300 hook invocations per configuration:
+
+| Health-gate implementation | SessionStart p50 |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Before: live `PRAGMA quick_check` and live FTS/body validation on the read path | 16.963810 ms |
+| After: recorded `quick_check` result, trigger-maintained `fts_rows`, and the body-length `CHECK` constraint | 1.016761 ms |
+
+These are measured subprocess hook times, not estimates. The after configuration
+moves `quick_check` to the write/session-end path; `SessionStart` reads its recorded
+result and uses the `fts_rows` counter, while SQLite enforces the body bound when a
+record is written.
